    board: rebind CF-218/CF-250/CF-254 completion evidence to the verdicts that judged them
    
    A sync-lane census of all 68 complete rows at tip 6bbb62b found three closures whose newest
    detail.evidence entry named only a run_id — no artifacts[] — so a stranger could neither open the
    judgement nor re-run anything:
    
      NO_ARTIFACT_LATEST CF-218 (run_id=9597368a)
      NO_ARTIFACT_LATEST CF-250 (run_id=bdfb4ce9)
      NO_ARTIFACT_LATEST CF-254 (run_id=abcc38ef)
    
    All three verdict directories exist and are already tracked at origin/main, so this is a binding
    gap, not missing evidence. Each row gained a SUPERSEDING evidence entry (historical entry kept
    intact, nothing erased) naming .gitreins/history/2026-11-05/<run>/verdict.json with
    --evidence-fingerprint = sha256sum of that file at the landed tip. No status, commit_hash or
    acceptance text was touched, and no task_completed event was emitted.
    
    Measured before -> after, same instrument, same tree:
      board-evidence-census.sh -> finding_lines=3 (all NO_ARTIFACT_LATEST) -> 0
      boardctl validate        -> RESULT: OK (4 pre-existing warnings) -> RESULT: OK (4 warnings)
      docs-status-drift.py     -> table_row_contradictions=0 -> 0
      verdict-binding-sweep.py -> orphan_count=1 (CF-077/410022a2 bound to 1dfb58b8aa, on no branch)
    
    Facts disclosed rather than smoothed over:
    - CF-218's own verdict 9597368a carries passed=false: Tier 2 COMPLETE with all three criteria
      PASS, the overall FAIL coming from the tree-wide python lint red that 52e1c4d introduced and
      CF-254 cleared at 0978d58. The row's status is unchanged by this tick; the note on the row says
      so. Flipping that row is a decision, not bookkeeping, and is left to its owner.
    - CF-250's verdict is bound to 3b2668e (a board commit landed after its implementation commit
      bd4c739 — lazy commit resolution in a shared checkout), which is on origin/main.
    - The remaining orphan (CF-077/410022a2 -> 1dfb58b8aa) is already tracked by pending row CF-181;
      it was re-measured at this tip, not re-filed.
    
    Gate position, stated exactly at the landed commit: this repo has no GitHub Actions workflow
    (gh run list -> [], so ci=SKIP, not green). bash scripts/boardctl validate -> RESULT: OK (4
    pre-existing warnings). bash tests/selftest.sh -> SELFTEST: PASS, rc=0, 324 PASS rows. That green
    is the REBASED tree: at the base tip 6bbb62b the same suite was red (SELFTEST: FAIL (1) — the §51
    arm asserting the tracked python surface is clean, ruff E401 from 6bbb62b's own
    `import subprocess, tempfile` in scripts/master_doc_fill.py, absent at its parent 584b550 and
    owned by pending row CF-257). Sibling commit 55ddb92 cleared that red mid-tick and this board
    commit was rebased onto it, which is why the gate now measures green; the red I first measured is
    recorded here rather than quietly dropped. guard=PASS on the rebased tree.
    
    Transport disclosed: the registered checkout was barriered — a sibling tick
    (code-factory-2026-11-05-15-11-56) held the board files staged and live, with CF-257 in_progress
    and a `timeout ... hermes chat` worker child running in that cwd — so the whole pass ran in a
    dedicated clone of origin/main at 6bbb62b under tick scratch
    (cfsync-laNCn2/cfclone). The candidate was not read for work, not written, and not cleaned. A
    fresh clone carries no installed hooks, so the configured checks were run by hand (validate +
    selftest) and this board-and-docs-only commit takes the CF-031 precedent.
    
