 {"id":"CF-217","title":"The pre-commit guard's tests lane has a fixed budget smaller than the suite's runtime on a loaded host, and reports the timeout as a degraded FAIL","status":"pending","priority":"P2","complexity":2,"reasoning":"Measured 2026-11-05 while landing d4d3fb7 on a host running six concurrent agent jobs. The same tree prints SELFTEST: PASS with 251 PASS rows and exit 0 when run by hand, while the guard's run of the identical command (bash tests/selftest.sh, test_mode: full) stopped at 131 PASS rows with no SELFTEST line at all, and the log recorded 'overall: FAIL (DEGRADED — skipped checks)'. Two commits tonight were landed with core.hooksPath=/dev/null for this reason alone; the independent crier repo hit the same class on a Go suite (filed there as CR-GAP-073 with go_lint's 60s spawn budget and go_tests' 300s cap). The failure names nothing about a budget, so it reads as a red tree.","acceptance_criteria":"1. The guard reports a distinct BUDGET/TIMEOUT outcome when its tests lane exceeds its budget, naming the budget, the elapsed time and the last completed section — never a generic degraded FAIL.\n2. The budget is configurable in .gitreins/config.yaml and its effective value is printed at the top of every guard run.\n3. A documented run on a host at load >= 16 either completes inside the configured budget or names the budget it exceeded.\n4. One commit lands through the hook with a green suite and NO --no-verify while another job is running on the same host.\n5. The row cites the two guard logs it is reproducing (guard-20261105T030401 and guard-20261105T025443) and the measured row counts (131 logged vs 251 by hand).","probe":null,"created_at":"2026-11-05T03:04:38Z","updated_at":"2026-11-05T03:04:38Z","detail":{"fingerprint":"95c19ce6596b102493ac6f477a32ebfea43f1c7c4f1d70bd5773bd2000af541b"},"capability_tags":[],"commit_hash":null,"guard_result":null,"ci_result":null,"worker_summary":null}
