 {"id":"CF-219","title":"No installer puts Go on a bunker: install-go.sh at a pin, verifying the toolchain can actually fetch a module","status":"complete","priority":"P0","complexity":2,"reasoning":"Same audit. scripts/harness/install-hermes.sh is the only measured installer and it installs a python package; there is no script that puts a Go toolchain under $HOME on a node, and layer 10 does not ask for one. A node without Go cannot run the tests of 27 of 61 fleet origins.","acceptance_criteria":"1. scripts/install-go.sh --check/--apply installs a pinned Go toolchain under $HOME, no root, no system package manager, and reads the version back.\n2. --apply proves the toolchain works beyond --version: it resolves a module through the proxy configuration the node will use (or FAILs naming the proxy).\n3. The install is idempotent: a second --apply changes nothing and says so.\n4. Provisioning calls it for Go-kind projects only, and --check names go as missing for those.","probe":null,"created_at":"2026-11-05T03:06:46Z","updated_at":"2026-11-05T15:15:51Z","detail":{"fingerprint":"4e95d2453a4d2f95415d46c8c4a08082a0d23dd9add2f131b1d2876c1457622c","evidence":[{"run_id":"3f14d5b8","ts":"2026-11-05T15:15:51Z","tree_fp":"89afa4e0fc824c9e8a81ffe1d2aec0491cadd7af072f43b787d9f200ed972f94","artifacts":[".gitreins/history/2026-11-05/3f14d5b8/verdict.json"]}]},"capability_tags":[],"commit_hash":"50e5f5b29e24b3cf631ebc61c6d38ac137391661","guard_result":"SKIP","ci_result":"SKIP","worker_summary":"Landed at 50e5f5b: scripts/install-go.sh pins go1.26.5 with the published per-arch sha256, installs below $HOME (no root, no apt), reads the version back, proves rsc.io/quote@v1.5.2 resolves through the node's GOPROXY with a cold module cache, and is idempotent. Layer 10 applies it only on --apply and only for kind sets that include go; node-create stages it. Selftest section 50 proves the missing / wrong-digest / positive arms and the full suite prints SELFTEST: PASS.","foreman_note":"GitRe