 {"id": "CF-220", "title": "Nothing seeds the prompts or the skills into a bunker, so the foreman we now run there has neither", "status": "complete", "priority": "P0", "complexity": 3, "reasoning": "Measured 2026-11-05: the repo carries prompts/ (11 lane prompts) and skills/ (code-factory-foreman, code-factory-bunker), and no script under scripts/ references either — node-create.sh stages project-node.sh, lib.sh, disk_floor.py, reclaim_disk.py and the harness adapter, nothing more. Since the foreman now runs INSIDE the bunker (topology 2.2), a node without prompts and skills improvises instead of following procedure. The audit measured the real skill library at ~9 MB (the 1.7 GB figure is curator backup tarballs, which must never be copied to a node).", "acceptance_criteria": "1. Provisioning seeds prompts/ and the declared skill set into the node under $HOME/.hermes, digest-recorded, and refuses to seed a file whose digest does not match the source.\n2. The seed is a declared list with a size budget (~16 MB), and a node's seed is reportable: what it has, its digest, when it was applied.\n3. A check row fails when the node's prompts/skills differ from the declared digests.\n4. Backup tarballs and the full user skill library are excluded by construction, and the row says how.", "probe": null, "created_at": "2026-11-05T03:06:46Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-05T13:20:52Z", "detail": {"evidence": [{"run_id": "diag-node-1-2026-11-05-cf220-live", "ts": "2026-11-05T13:15:08Z", "tree_fp": "fd84f1db62e4b0f2dcdc9f06eeba50617f1473c4", "artifacts": ["docs/audits/code-factory-cf220-2026-11-05.md"]}, {"run_id": "e6f97b34", "ts": "2026-11-05T13:20:52Z", "tree_fp": "c109421a0bb86f527fcd905dc732ca33b0c8e824", "artifacts": ["docs/audits/code-factory-cf220-2026-11-05.md", ".gitreins/history/2026-11-05/e6f97b34/verdict.json"], "note": "Tier-2 judge CF-220-R1, lane ollama-cloud/glm-5.3-flash, passed=true at commit ce86ca3"}]}, "capability_tags": [], "commit_hash": "b3ed55cd944bccece799be5f79d0895bd9881293", "guard_result": "PASS", "ci_result": "SKIP", "worker_summary": "node_seed.py seeds a declared list (config/node-seed.txt: 11 prompts + 2 skills) into $HOME/.hermes with a sha256 per file; apply verifies every digest BEFORE installing and refuses the whole seed on one mismatch; check compares disk to record and exits 1 naming each drifted path; provisioning runs it as stage 4b. Closed by verification on 2026-11-05: cf-node carries 13 seeded files plus seed-applied.json (applied_at 2026-11-05T04:52:15Z), check green, red and named after one appended line, green again after restore; selftest node_seed section 6/6 arms PASS.", "foreman_note": "VERIFICATION-ONLY CLOSEOUT 2026-11-05 (diag-node-1 tick). The implementation landed at b3ed55c and was pushed the night before this tick; the row was left in_progress with no closeout, so this tick ran the criteria instead of redispatching the work. Live on cf-node (bunker-las-03): 13 seeded files plus $HOME/.hermes/seed-applied.json (applied_at 2026-11-05T04:52:15Z); `node_seed.py check` PASS 13/13; after appending one line to prompts/foreman.md, FAIL naming `prompts/foreman.md drifted (75da16fb93fd != 82c020b6f316)` and exit 1; after restoring the file from a node-side backup taken in the same run, PASS 13/13 and exit 0 — so the node is left exactly as the seed wrote it. Fixture gate at the judged tip: `bash tests/selftest.sh` -> SELFTEST: PASS with the node_seed section's six arms. ci_result is SKIP because this repo carries no .github/workflows: `gh run list --repo coding-hermes/code-factory --limit 3` returns [] and the local guard is the gate. Residual filed as CF-250: verify-node.sh has no seed leg, so control-host drift visibility for the seed does not exist yet.", "worker_status": "complete", "completed_at": "2026-11-05T13:15:08Z"}
 {"id":"CF-221","title":"oh-my-pi (omp) needs bun, not node, and nothing installs either: an installer at @oh-my-pi/pi-coding-agent@18.16.0","status":"pending","priority":"P2","complexity":2,"reasoning":"Toolchain audit 2026-11-05, web-verified: oh-my-pi is the npm package @oh-my-pi/pi-coding-agent 18.16.0, binary 'omp', 12 packages / 72.8 MB plus puppeteer-core and axe-core (~82 MB), and its engine is bun >= 1.4.4 — installing it on node silently fails or half-works. Upstream's 'curl omp.sh/install | sh' is banned by this repo's own rule (lib.sh:18 never pipes to a shell).","acceptance_criteria":"1. scripts/install-omp.sh --check/--apply installs the pinned package under $HOME and reads 'omp --version' back.\n2. --check FAILs naming bun when bun < 1.4.4 is absent, instead of letting npm install something that cannot run.\n3. Idempotent: a second --apply reports no change and the binary digest is unchanged.\n4. The install path is a package manager, never a piped installer script.","probe":null,"created_at":"2026-11-05T03:06:54Z","updated_at":"2026-11-05T03:06:54Z","detail":{"fingerprint":"effe074e064e2dcdd24b49a4233f2ec1cf95acf464a0e47445238e203fac131e"},"capability_tags":[],"commit_hash":null,"guard_result":null,"ci_result":null,"worker_summary":null}
