 {"id": "CF-255", "title": "P2 — the gitreins Tier-2 judge lane is unfunded: the deepseek balance is -$0.87 and every judge run on the default lane writes an INCOMPLETE 402 verdict", "status": "pending", "priority": "P2", "complexity": 1, "reasoning": "Measured 2026-11-05T09:26Z. `gitreins task complete CF-218` printed \"Evaluator error: LLM call failed: 402 Client Error: Payment Required for url: https://api.deepseek.com/v1/chat/completions (provider=openai model=deepseek-v4-flash)\", saved verdict 94c31d59 (tier 1 PASS, tier 2 judged nothing) and exited 1. The provider probe attributes it to balance, not credentials: `curl .../user/balance` returns {\"is_available\":false,\"balance_infos\":[{\"currency\":\"USD\",\"total_balance\":\"-0.87\",\"topped_up_balance\":\"-0.87\"}]}. The same task was then judged with a per-invocation override onto the ambient fireworks judge key (base https://api.fireworks.ai/inference/v1, model accounts/fireworks/models/kimi-k3, chat probe 200) and Tier 2 came back COMPLETE twice (verdicts 0e9f844d, 9597368a). So today every row that wants LLM judgement needs a manual failover, and a run without one writes an INCOMPLETE verdict into history that later readers must classify by hand.", "acceptance_criteria": "1. One probe decides the state and is quoted in the row: `curl -s -H \"Authorization: Bearer $GITREINS_LLM_API_KEY\" https://api.deepseek.com/user/balance` returns is_available=true with a positive balance, OR the fleet's gitreins default LLM lane (GITREINS_LLM_BASE_URL/MODEL/KEY source, or .gitreins/config.yaml) names a funded endpoint — the row records which of the two was chosen and the file that carries it.\n2. A fresh `gitreins task complete <id>` on a small row produces a verdict dir whose summary carries no \"402\" line and whose tier 2 reads COMPLETE; the row cites that verdict directory id.\n3. The failover set that worked (base URL, model id, key variable name) is recorded so the next tick does not re-derive it, and it is NOT made durable without the owner's word.", "created_at": "2026-11-05T14:41:36Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-05T14:41:36Z", "detail": {"fingerprint": "c8cb80269758051b82b58bce96e517bd0f1aaa9e729fda7c6884aaff3f6448e8"}, "foreman_note": null}
 {"id": "CF-256", "title": "P3 — the diag-node-1 lane prompt names a workdir that exists on no host: /home/bunker-cf-node/code-factory (the node's checkout is /home/bunker-cf-node/repo)", "status": "pending", "priority": "P3", "complexity": 1, "reasoning": "Measured 2026-11-05T14:46Z by the diag-node-1 tick itself: its prompt ends 'Workdir: /home/bunker-cf-node/code-factory'. On the control host realpath of that path is 'No such file or directory' and $(id -un) is kara with cwd /home/kara, so the locator cannot be honoured there; on cf-node (bunker-las-03, 100.69.3.13) the same path is absent while the node's real checkout is /home/bunker-cf-node/repo at 2889c52 (git rev-parse --show-toplevel from the node, same tick). A lane that trusts the locator either stops as a routing failure or silently works in a different tree. Sibling rows cover node checkout drift (CF-248) and the node harness (CF-249/CF-253); none covers the prompt's own path.", "acceptance_criteria": "1. The generator of the diag-node-1 lane prompt names a workdir that exists: for a control-host tick it names the registered checkout (/home/kara/code-factory per the scheduler projects row) and for a node-side tick it names the node's measured checkout path. 2. A check FAILS when a lane prompt names a workdir whose realpath is not a git toplevel, and prints the path it measured, so this cannot regress silently. 3. The row records which generator was corrected and which tick id first carried the corrected locator.", "created_at": "2026-11-05T15:17:08Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-05T15:17:08Z", "detail": {"fingerprint": "dbfcc50423299b8c7978ac169b8a299c1f6fd6c1f70850e0947b704ac7d6f49f"}, "foreman_note": null}
 {"id": "CF-257", "title": "P2 - the master-doc fill program cannot converge: the marker it selects on is still present in files it has already filled, so every run re-fills all 41 modules", "status": "in_progress", "priority": "P2", "complexity": 2, "reasoning": "Measured 2026-11-05 by the diag-node-1 tick. scripts/master_doc_fill.py treats a module as todo when its text contains \"RED - no verification recorded\" (main(), the selector at the --force line). Filling does NOT clear that string: it is the template Status row, and docs/master/01-scripts-add-family-lanes-py.md - filled today, 8921 chars of cited content - still matches it, as do 39 of the 41 files the [0-9][0-9]-*.md glob selects. Consequence measured on the live batch: `python3 scripts/master_doc_fill.py --provider deepseek --workers 3` (pid 3471633, started 10:03) printed todo=41 and has been re-writing already-filled modules for 31 minutes at ~158 s per module (module 05 alone: 4537 chars in 158 s), so a pass costs ~100+ minutes and no run can ever finish the program. The same defect makes --force meaningless. Also measured: the glob matches 00-INDEX.md, which is not a module and would be sent to a model as one. Separately, module 05 shipped six lines of construction narration (\"Maybe too many rows; okay.\") from a batch that predated the NARRATION refusal that landed in 0978d58, so outputs from any batch started before that commit are unguarded.", "acceptance_criteria": "1. The selector reads a completion marker a fill actually writes: on a fully filled tree a fresh run prints todo=0 and changes no file, and the row quotes the two run outputs (before and after) plus the marker it reads. 2. Two consecutive runs on a filled tree are idempotent: exit 0, no content or byte change in docs/master (AGENTS.md rule 5). 3. docs/master/00-INDEX.md is excluded from the module glob, or handled explicitly as an index rather than sent to a model: the row shows the match it makes today and the guard that stops it. 4. The narration rule (scripts/master_doc_fill.py NARRATION) returns 0 hits over docs/master at the close, including modules written by any batch started before 0978d58, with the grep command and count quoted. 5. bash tests/selftest.sh prints SELFTEST: PASS and bash docs/audits/cf198-section-mapping.sh prints RESULT: OK at the commit the row closes on.", "created_at": "2026-11-05T15:34:33Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-05T16:05:47Z", "detail": {"fingerprint": "4369cdcfc057df9817bda01a9dbbdccbf64b4a6fc86522509d28ff7d0ac26f15"}, "foreman_note": "foreman tick code-factory-2026-11-05-15-11-56 claims this row. Base: 6bbb62b. Measured at claim: 39 of 41 docs/master modules still carry the template Status row 'RED — no verification recorded'; the glob [0-9][0-9]-*.md still matches 00-INDEX.md; scripts/master_doc_fill.py as landed in 6bbb62b is red on the Tier-1 lint arm (ruff E401 at scripts/master_doc_fill.py:292, import subprocess, tempfile) and off-format, so any commit staging it is refused — clearing both is part of this row's fix, as CF-254 set the rule."}
